From b773e0e900f47645dd7e03db4abc864d9f91f458 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 21:00:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05519/11362] [outer-loop] fix _flips_gate word-boundary bug
 that falsely flagged exp5173's blocked DiffusionGemma pilot

User: 'dig into it' (the CIRCULAR_MOAT_OVERCLAIM flag on .474's DiffusionGemma pilot).

results/experiment_5173_diffusiongemma_energy_guided_diffusion_pilot_v474.json was
CRITICAL-flagged (CIRCULAR_MOAT_OVERCLAIM, MOAT_CLAIM_RIGOR) despite its own
honest_verdict correctly starting with blocked_ -- the pilot never ran (arm_rows=[],
every pass_at_1_* field is a degenerate 0.0 placeholder, the smoke test itself
failed on a device-placement error before any arm could execute).

Root cause: _flips_gate() did a plain 'diffusiongemma_met' in honest_verdict.lower()
substring check. The verdict text 'blocked_diffusiongemma_meta_tensor_bug_unresolved'
contains 'diffusiongemma_meta_tensor' -- 'meta' starts with 'met', a pure substring
coincidence with nothing to do with any gate being MET (meta tensor is a real
PyTorch term for placeholder tensors during device-mapped model loading). The
artifact never claimed anything; the linter manufactured a claim from a technical
term.

Fixed with word-boundary-aware regexes (_GATE_MET_RE, _DIFFUSIONGEMMA_MET_RE)
requiring 'met' not be immediately followed by another lowercase letter/digit --
excludes meta/method/metric/metadata while still matching the genuine word 'met'
at a token boundary (followed by '_' or end-of-string). Verified against real
corpus patterns before committing: the genuine 'gate_MET' usages in
experiment_4347/4346 (the moat-replicated/leak-robust archive and capstone
artifacts) still detect correctly.

11 new tests (tests/python/test_adversarial_verify_flips_gate_word_boundary.py):
unit coverage of the word-boundary edge cases (meta/method/metric exclusions,
genuine matches at underscore and string-end boundaries, the dict-form
diffusiongemma_gate checks) plus an exact reproduction of the exp5173
false-positive now clean, plus a regression guard confirming a genuinely
circular gate-flip claim is still caught. Full existing suite (234 tests)
stays green. Live re-check on exp5173 itself: 0 flags (was 2 CRITICAL).
Scanned all 48 directly-relevant diffusiongemma/moat-named artifacts: only 2
remain flagged, both pre-existing WARN-severity (the check's intended,
non-blocking behavior), no CRITICAL false positives left.

exp5173's own substance is unchanged by this correction: the pilot is still
genuinely blocked on the June-14-vintage meta-tensor loading bug, which
requires DiffusionGemma's dedicated diffusion API (not the standard
causal-LM forward interface) to actually run.

